1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:37,000
青い風が今 群れのドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:51,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で 運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

4
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

6
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の体勢 窓辺からやがて取り立つ

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:21,000
ほとばしる 熱いパックスで 想い出を裏切るなら

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:29,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

9
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
ご視聴ありがとうございました

10
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:39,000
さんの国民のスムープに戻って discuss for aung Score シャコンで欲しい

11
00:01:39,000 --> 00:02:02,160
クリーフiiつため 歌謀な

12
00:02:02,160 --> 00:02:05,160
With a heart that can't be mended, ha-ha-ha.

13
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,160
All right.

14
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:08,160
Let's do it, ha-ha.

15
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:10,160
Oh, my gosh.

16
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:12,160
Did you hear all that gossip?

17
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:15,160
Asuka, Asuka, Asuka.

18
00:02:15,160 --> 00:02:17,160
They're totally clueless.

19
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:19,160
Thanks, come again.

20
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:23,160
At least your pictures don't reveal her personality.

21
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,160
Hello.

22
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:28,160
Guten Morgen, Chinji.

23
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:30,160
Guten Morgen.

24
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:32,160
Hey, why so gloomy?

25
00:02:32,160 --> 00:02:35,160
I'm the most popular girl in school.

26
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:38,160
You should appreciate your good fortune.

27
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:41,160
Hey, the other one's here too, isn't she?

28
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:42,160
Other one?

29
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,160
What are you, stupid?

30
00:02:44,160 --> 00:02:46,160
I'm talking about the first child, of course.

31
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:48,160
Oh, Ayanami.

32
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,160
Hm?

33
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:50,160
Hello.

34
00:02:50,160 --> 00:03:03,160
You must be Rei Ayanami, the pilot of the prototype.

35
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,160
I'm Asuka.

36
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:08,160
Asuka Langley Soryu.

37
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,160
I'm the designated pilot of Ava 2.

38
00:03:10,160 --> 00:03:11,160
Let's be good friends.

39
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,160
What for?

40
00:03:12,160 --> 00:03:14,160
Because it would be convenient.

41
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:16,160
You know what I mean.

42
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,160
If I'm ordered to, I will do it.

43
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:20,160
Ooh, freakazoid.

44
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:22,160
It takes one to know one.

45
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:25,160
I wonder if only weirdos are chosen to be Ava pilots.

46
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:26,160
Oh!

47
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,160
You've lost some weight.

48
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,160
Oh?

49
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:29,160
You're enduring an unrequited love.

50
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:30,160
Really?

51
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,160
You're so very sure, are you?

52
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,160
Hmm.

53
00:03:33,160 --> 00:03:38,160
A woman with a mole like a tear on her cheek is destined to a life full of heartache and sorrow.

54
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:56,160
If you're trying to put the moves on me, I'm afraid you can't. Not while that face is pressed against the glass anyway.

55
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,160
It's been quite a while, Kashi.

56
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,160
It's been a while, all right.

57
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,160
You know, you're not as discreet as I remember.

58
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,160
He ain't never been discreet as I remember.

59
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,160
He ain't never been discreet as I remember.

60
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,160
You've finished handing over Unit 2, haven't you?

61
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:07,160
What are you still doing here?

62
00:04:07,160 --> 00:04:15,160
I received orders this morning that I'll be staying around so, Gorgeous, we can hang around again, just like we used to.

63
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,160
Oh, don't flatter yourself.

64
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,160
Enemy attack?

65
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,160
We've just received this report from the battlecruiser Haruna.

66
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:22,160
Have detected huge submerged object off the Ki'i Peninsula.

67
00:04:22,160 --> 00:04:23,160
Sending data.

68
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,160
Got it.

69
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,160
The data has been analyzed.

70
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,160
We've just received this report from the battlecruiser Haruna.

71
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,160
Have detected huge submerged object off the Ki'i Peninsula.

72
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,160
Sending data.

73
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,160
Got it.

74
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,160
The data has been analyzed.

75
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:36,160
The wavelength pattern confirms it.

76
00:04:36,160 --> 00:04:37,160
It's an angel.

77
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:40,160
All personnel, go to first stage alert.

78
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:48,160
The recent battle has severely damaged Tokyo-3's intercept system.

79
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:51,160
Only 26% of our defense capability has been restored.

80
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:56,160
In addition, our operational capability for actual combat is virtually nil.

81
00:04:56,160 --> 00:05:01,160
Therefore, we're going to have to intercept the target at the water's edge right before it makes land.

82
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:05,160
Units one and two will mount a coordinated attack in a series of waves.

83
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,160
In other words, close in and take turns.

84
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,160
Roger.

85
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,160
This sucks.

86
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:12,160
My first fight over Japan and she won't let me handle it solo.

87
00:05:12,160 --> 00:05:14,160
Why do I have to bring you?

88
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:15,160
S.O.P.

89
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:17,160
That's just procedures, you know.

90
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:20,160
Well, let me tell you something first, third child.

91
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,160
Just don't get in my way.

92
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:26,160
Hmm, his selection as a pilot must have been a joke, right?

93
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:42,160
Two against one's not what I'd call a fair fight.

94
00:05:42,160 --> 00:05:43,160
It's not fair.

95
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:44,160
We don't get a choice.

96
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:46,160
Survivability takes priority.

97
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:52,160
Huh?

98
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,160
There.

99
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,160
Beginning attack!

100
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:02,160
I'll handle this angle.

101
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,160
Cover my back, Shinji!

102
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,160
C-Cover you?

103
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,160
Yeah!

104
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,160
Ladies first!

105
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,160
Dammit!

106
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:09,160
Don't you talk to me like that, you dumb rookie!

107
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,160
In charge!

108
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:16,160
What?

109
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,160
Well, I'll be damned.

110
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:35,160
Well, what did you think of that?

111
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:38,160
A fight should be clean and elegant without waste.

112
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,160
What?

113
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,160
What?

114
00:06:43,160 --> 00:06:44,160
What?

115
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,160
That's a load of bull!

116
00:06:55,160 --> 00:07:04,160
Today at 10.58, 15 seconds AM, Unit 1 was attacked by one of the targets, Alpha, which had separated from the other target, submerged two kilometers off Cerber Mubei.

117
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:09,160
20 seconds later, Unit 2 was stopped by Target Beta's attack.

118
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:12,160
I believe the project chairperson summed it up best.

119
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,160
This is pathetic!

120
00:07:16,160 --> 00:07:18,160
This is all your fault!

121
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,160
You totally screwed up my debut battle!

122
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:21,160
What are you talking about?

123
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,160
What are you talking about?

124
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:24,160
You're the one who charged in there acting like an idiot!

125
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,160
Idiot?

126
00:07:25,160 --> 00:07:28,160
How dare you call me that, you pathetic excuse for a combat pilot!

127
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,160
You're just a jerk!

128
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:30,160
Me?

129
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,160
You were in such a rush to show off, you disregarded procedure!

130
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,160
What was that?!

131
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:34,160
What was that?!

132
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:35,160
You look like a drowned rat!

133
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,160
Hmph!

134
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,160
You, you can't say that kind of thing to me!

135
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:42,160
NERV abandoning operation and transferred command to UN secondary force.

136
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:44,160
We've been completely humiliated!

137
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:48,160
At 11.05 AM, the UN forces made an attack with an in-tune mind.

138
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,160
We'll have to redraw the map again.

139
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:53,160
They succeeded in burning off 28% of the target's structural substance.

140
00:07:53,160 --> 00:07:55,160
Well, it kinda looks dead.

141
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:58,160
This is merely temporary. The second attack is just a matter of time.

142
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:03,160
Well, at least we've got time to regroup and you can't ask for more than that.

143
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:07,160
Alright, you two. Just what do you think your job is?

144
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:08,160
Piloting Ava?

145
00:08:08,160 --> 00:08:10,160
Wrong! It's to beat the angels!

146
00:08:10,160 --> 00:08:14,160
NERV does not exist to make grotesque public spectacles like this!

147
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:17,160
Therefore, the two of you will learn to work together!

148
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:18,160
Why should we?!

149
00:08:18,160 --> 00:08:20,160
Enough!

150
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:25,160
Why does everyone get so angry here?

151
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:27,160
Adults have a thing about credibility.

152
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:30,160
Um, where's Misato?

153
00:08:30,160 --> 00:08:31,160
Clearing things up.

154
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:35,160
It's the duty of the person in charge to take responsibility for anything that goes wrong.

155
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,160
Oh, look what we have here.

156
00:08:37,160 --> 00:08:40,160
Here are the protests and damage reports from all of the bureaus concerned.

157
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:42,160
This is a bill from the UN.

158
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,160
And you've got a complaint from public relations as well.

159
00:08:44,160 --> 00:08:46,160
I hope you have fun reading them all.

160
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:48,160
I already know what they say.

161
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:51,160
If you're going to fight, please don't do it here, right?

162
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:53,160
I'd say that was a good guess.

163
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:56,160
I'll do it after we kill this angel. I will destroy it.

164
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:57,160
That would be a nice start.

165
00:08:57,160 --> 00:09:01,160
I think you should know that Commander Fuyutsuki isn't exactly happy with this whole situation.

166
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:05,160
I'm afraid you could be busted back to Lieutenant, or even lower.

167
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:09,160
I guess it was just good luck within bad luck that Commander Ikari wasn't here.

168
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:12,160
If he'd been here, you'd have already been fired.

169
00:09:12,160 --> 00:09:17,160
So you've brought me some ideas to help save my job, haven't you, dear friend?

170
00:09:17,160 --> 00:09:18,160
Like this one?

171
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:21,160
Ah, I thank you, Dr. Ritsugu Akagi.

172
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:23,160
It's good to have a friend you can count on.

173
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:24,160
That's nice.

174
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:27,160
But I'm not the one who'll be saving your backside this time.

175
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:29,160
This is Mr. Kaji's idea.

176
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,160
Kaji?

177
00:09:31,160 --> 00:09:47,160
I'm home!

178
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:50,160
Not that anyone's here, of course, but...

179
00:09:50,160 --> 00:09:53,160
What?! What is this?!

180
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:57,160
Don't be so rude! These are my personal belongings!

181
00:09:57,160 --> 00:09:58,160
You?!

182
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,160
But what in the blazes are you doing in my house?!

183
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:02,160
Why are you still here?

184
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:03,160
Still here?!

185
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,160
Don't...

186
00:10:04,160 --> 00:10:07,160
Hmm, yeah, you've been dumped for the new model.

187
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:10,160
Misato will be living with me.

188
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:14,160
Of course, that's a much more logical choice when you consider my superior abilities.

189
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:17,160
Although, honestly, I'd rather live with Kaji.

190
00:10:17,160 --> 00:10:20,160
Say, just why are Japanese houses so small, anyway?

191
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:23,160
I couldn't even get half my stuff in my new room!

192
00:10:23,160 --> 00:10:28,160
And Japanese sure don't have any sense of privacy.

193
00:10:28,160 --> 00:10:31,160
How can they live in a room without locks?!

194
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,160
Unbelievable!

195
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,160
It's weird.

196
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:38,160
The Japanese way is to consider the needs of others before one's own.

197
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:40,160
Misato, how's it going?

198
00:10:40,160 --> 00:10:43,160
You two are going to get along real well.

199
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:44,160
What?

200
00:10:44,160 --> 00:10:45,160
Just what do you mean?

201
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:46,160
This is part of your new training.

202
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:47,160
Say what?!

203
00:10:47,160 --> 00:10:51,160
There is only one way to destroy the seventh angel.

204
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:56,160
Execute a simultaneous two-point attack on each target's core while the angel is separated.

205
00:10:56,160 --> 00:10:57,160
Oh.

206
00:10:57,160 --> 00:11:02,160
In other words, an attack on both halves by two Evas with perfectly synchronized timing.

207
00:11:02,160 --> 00:11:06,160
Coordination between the two of you will be vital to the success of the mission.

208
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:07,160
Huh?

209
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:10,160
To that end, I want the two of you to live together from now on.

210
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,160
No way!

211
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:16,160
A boy and a girl should never sleep under one roof after the age of seven!

212
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:19,160
The angel is currently regenerating itself.

213
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:21,160
It will begin its second assault in six days.

214
00:11:21,160 --> 00:11:23,160
But it's impossible.

215
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:26,160
We have a way of making it possible.

216
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:30,160
The master attack pattern will be choreographed using this music.

217
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:35,160
If you follow it exactly, you will be able to work in sync and completely destroy both targets.

218
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:36,160
We begin now.

219
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:38,160
We attack in six days.

220
00:11:38,160 --> 00:11:49,160
I'm getting really worried about Shinji.

221
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,160
He's been gone for three days, hasn't he?

222
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:57,160
Hey, it's the class rep.

223
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:59,160
Two of the three stitches.

224
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:00,160
So, why are you here?

225
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,160
To see on the story he was doing.

226
00:12:01,160 --> 00:12:02,160
What about you?

227
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:03,160
To look in on Shinji.

228
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,160
Why did you stop here?

229
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:05,160
Coming.

230
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:06,160
Hmm?

231
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:07,160
You betrayed us.

232
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:08,160
You're dressing alike again, too.

233
00:12:08,160 --> 00:12:09,160
I can't believe this.

234
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,160
Neither can we.

235
00:12:10,160 --> 00:12:11,160
It's all Misada's fault.

236
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:13,160
We have to eat, breathe and sleep together.

237
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,160
Huh?

238
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:15,160
You're living in sin.

239
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:16,160
That's awful.

240
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,160
No, it's not like that.

241
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:18,160
Ugh.

242
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:19,160
It's just what is it like?

243
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,160
Hi, everybody.

244
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,160
Would you like to explain all of this to us?

245
00:12:21,160 --> 00:12:22,160
Geez, Shinji.

246
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,160
You should have told us about that part first.

247
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:24,160
So, how are there coordination drills coming along, Miss Misato?

248
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,160
Not very well, as you can see.

249
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,160
No.

250
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:27,160
No.

251
00:12:27,160 --> 00:12:28,160
We'll stop.

252
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,160
Not very well, as you can see.

253
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,160
Yes, I can't do.

254
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:31,160
No, I can't do.

255
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:32,160
I can't do.

256
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,160
No.

257
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,160
No.

258
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:35,160
No.

259
00:12:35,160 --> 00:12:36,160
I can't believe this.

260
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:37,160
Neither can we.

261
00:12:37,160 --> 00:12:38,160
It's all Misada's fault.

262
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,160
